id: form-composition
title: Form Composition
---
NIFT_TANSTACK_DOCUMENT_V1
{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A common criticism of TanStack Form is its verbosity out-of-the-box. While this "},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"can"}]},{"type":"text","value":" be useful for educational purposes - helping enforce understanding our APIs - it's not ideal in production use cases."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"As a result, while basic usage of "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"[tanstackField]"},{"type":"text","value":" enables the most powerful and flexible usage of TanStack Form, we provide APIs that wrap it and make your application code less verbose."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"pre-bound-field-components","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Pre-bound Field Components"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"If you've ever used TanStack Form in Angular to bind more than one input, you'll have quickly realized how much goes into each input:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { Component } from '@angular/core'\nimport { TanStackField, injectForm, injectStore } from '@tanstack/angular-form'\n\n@Component({\n  selector: 'app-root',\n  standalone: true,\n  imports: [TanStackField],\n  template: `\n    <div>\n      <ng-container [tanstackField]=\"form\" name=\"firstName\" #firstName=\"field\">\n        <label [for]=\"firstName.api.name\">First Name:</label>\n        <input\n          [id]=\"firstName.api.name\"\n          [name]=\"firstName.api.name\"\n          [value]=\"firstName.api.state.value\"\n          (blur)=\"firstName.api.handleBlur()\"\n          (input)=\"firstName.api.handleChange($any($event).target.value)\"\n        />\n        @if (firstName.api.state.meta.isTouched) {\n          @for (error of firstName.api.state.meta.errors; track $index) {\n            <div style=\"color: red\">\n              {{ error }}\n            </div>\n          }\n        }\n        @if (firstName.api.state.meta.isValidating) {\n          <p>Validating...</p>\n        }\n      </ng-container>\n    </div>\n    <div>\n      <ng-container [tanstackField]=\"form\" name=\"lastName\" #lastName=\"field\">\n        <label [for]=\"lastName.api.name\">Last Name:</label>\n        <input\n          [id]=\"lastName.api.name\"\n          [name]=\"lastName.api.name\"\n          [value]=\"lastName.api.state.value\"\n          (blur)=\"lastName.api.handleBlur()\"\n          (input)=\"lastName.api.handleChange($any($event).target.value)\"\n        />\n        @if (lastName.api.state.meta.isTouched) {\n          @for (error of lastName.api.state.meta.errors; track $index) {\n            <div style=\"color: red\">\n              {{ error }}\n            </div>\n          }\n        }\n        @if (lastName.api.state.meta.isValidating) {\n          <p>Validating...</p>\n        }\n      </ng-container>\n    </div>\n  `,\n})\nexport class AppComponent {\n  form = injectForm({\n    defaultValues: {\n      firstName: '',\n      lastName: '',\n    },\n    onSubmit({ value }) {\n      // Do something with form data\n      console.log(value)\n    },\n  })\n}","lang":"angular-ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This is functionally correct, but introduces a "},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"lot"}]},{"type":"text","value":" of repeated templating behavior over and over. Instead, let's move the error handling, label to input binding, and other repeated logic into a component:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { injectField } from '@tanstack/angular-form'\n\n@Component({\n  selector: 'app-text-field',\n  standalone: true,\n  template: `\n    <label [for]=\"field.api.name\">{{ label() }}</label>\n    <input\n      [id]=\"field.api.name\"\n      [name]=\"field.api.name\"\n      [value]=\"field.api.state.value\"\n      (blur)=\"field.api.handleBlur()\"\n      (input)=\"field.api.handleChange($any($event).target.value)\"\n    />\n    @if (field.api.state.meta.isTouched) {\n      @for (error of field.api.state.meta.errors; track $index) {\n        <div style=\"color: red\">\n          {{ error }}\n        </div>\n      }\n    }\n    @if (field.api.state.meta.isValidating) {\n      <p>Validating...</p>\n    }\n  `,\n})\nexport class AppTextField {\n  label = input.required<string>()\n  // This API requires another part to it from the parent component\n  field = injectField<string>()\n}","lang":"angular-ts"},{"type":"blockquote","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"injectField"},{"type":"text","value":" accepts a single generic to define the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"field.state.value"},{"type":"text","value":" type."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"As a result, a numerical text field would be represented as "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"injectField<number>"},{"type":"text","value":", for example."}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Now, we can use the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TanStackAppField"},{"type":"text","value":" directive ("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"tanstack-app-field"},{"type":"text","value":") to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"provide"},{"type":"text","value":" the expected field associated with this input:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { Component } from '@angular/core'\nimport {\n  TanStackAppField,\n  TanStackField,\n  injectForm,\n} from '@tanstack/angular-form'\n\n@Component({\n  selector: 'app-root',\n  standalone: true,\n  imports: [TanStackField, TanStackAppField, AppTextField],\n  template: `\n    <div>\n      <app-text-field\n        label=\"First name:\"\n        tanstack-app-field\n        [tanstackField]=\"form\"\n        name=\"firstName\"\n      />\n    </div>\n    <div>\n      <app-text-field\n        label=\"Last name:\"\n        tanstack-app-field\n        [tanstackField]=\"form\"\n        name=\"lastName\"\n      />\n    </div>\n  `,\n})\nexport class AppComponent {\n  form = injectForm({\n    defaultValues: {\n      firstName: '',\n      lastName: '',\n    },\n    onSubmit({ value }) {\n      // Do something with form data\n      console.log(value)\n    },\n  })\n}","lang":"angular-ts"},{"type":"blockquote","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Here, the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"tanstack-app-field"},{"type":"text","value":" directive is taking the properties from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"[tanstackField]"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"provide"},{"type":"text","value":"ing them down to the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"app-text-field"},{"type":"text","value":" so that they can be more easily consumed as a component."}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"breaking-big-forms-into-smaller-pieces","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Breaking big forms into smaller pieces"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Sometimes forms get very large; it's just how it goes sometimes. While TanStack Form supports large forms well, it's never fun to work with hundreds or thousands of lines of code in a single component."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"To solve this, we support breaking forms into smaller pieces using the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"[tanstack-with-form]"},{"type":"text","value":" directive together with the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"injectWithForm"},{"type":"text","value":" function."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The parent component owns the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"form"},{"type":"text","value":" (created via "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"injectForm"},{"type":"text","value":") and passes it down to a child component using the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"tanstack-with-form"},{"type":"text","value":" directive. The child component reads it back via "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"injectWithForm"},{"type":"text","value":", which returns a fully-typed reference to that same "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"FormApi"},{"type":"text","value":" — meaning the child can render "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"[tanstackField]"},{"type":"text","value":" bindings, "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"tanstack-app-field"},{"type":"text","value":" components, etc. against the parent's form without needing to redeclare any generics."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"First, lift your shared form options out using "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"formOptions"},{"type":"text","value":" so both the parent and the child can reference the same shape:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"// shared-form.ts\nimport { formOptions } from '@tanstack/angular-form'\n\nexport const peopleFormOpts = formOptions({\n  defaultValues: {\n    firstName: '',\n    lastName: '',\n  },\n})","lang":"angular-ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Then, build a child component that consumes the form via "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"injectWithForm"},{"type":"text","value":":"}]},{"type":"code","value":"// child-form.component.ts\nimport { Component } from '@angular/core'\nimport {\n  TanStackAppField,\n  TanStackField,\n  injectWithForm,\n} from '@tanstack/angular-form'\nimport { AppTextField } from './app-text-field.component'\nimport { peopleFormOpts } from './shared-form'\n\n@Component({\n  selector: 'app-child-form',\n  standalone: true,\n  imports: [TanStackField, TanStackAppField, AppTextField],\n  template: `\n    <app-text-field\n      label=\"First name:\"\n      tanstack-app-field\n      [tanstackField]=\"withForm.form\"\n      name=\"firstName\"\n    />\n    <app-text-field\n      label=\"Last name:\"\n      tanstack-app-field\n      [tanstackField]=\"withForm.form\"\n      name=\"lastName\"\n    />\n  `,\n})\nexport class ChildForm {\n  // Spreading the form options into `injectWithForm` is what gives `withForm.form`\n  // its full type inference — no generics needed.\n  withForm = injectWithForm({ ...peopleFormOpts })\n}","lang":"angular-ts"},{"type":"blockquote","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The options passed to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"injectWithForm({ ...peopleFormOpts })"},{"type":"text","value":" are only used for type inference. They are not read at runtime; the actual "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"FormApi"},{"type":"text","value":" instance comes from the ancestor "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"tanstack-with-form"},{"type":"text","value":" directive."}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Finally, in the parent component, create the form with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"injectForm"},{"type":"text","value":" and pass it to the child via the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"tanstack-with-form"},{"type":"text","value":" directive:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"// app.component.ts\nimport { Component } from '@angular/core'\nimport { TanStackWithForm, injectForm } from '@tanstack/angular-form'\nimport { ChildForm } from './child-form.component'\nimport { peopleFormOpts } from './shared-form'\n\n@Component({\n  selector: 'app-root',\n  standalone: true,\n  imports: [TanStackWithForm, ChildForm],\n  template: `\n    <form (submit)=\"handleSubmit($event)\">\n      <app-child-form tanstack-with-form [form]=\"form\" />\n      <button type=\"submit\">Submit</button>\n    </form>\n  `,\n})\nexport class AppComponent {\n  form = injectForm({\n    ...peopleFormOpts,\n    onSubmit({ value }) {\n      console.log(value)\n    },\n  })\n\n  handleSubmit(event: SubmitEvent) {\n    event.preventDefault()\n    event.stopPropagation()\n    this.form.handleSubmit()\n  }\n}","lang":"angular-ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This pattern lets you split a large form across many components while keeping a single source of truth for the form's state and types. Any descendant of the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"tanstack-with-form"},{"type":"text","value":" directive can call "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"injectWithForm({ ...peopleFormOpts })"},{"type":"text","value":" to gain typed access to the same form instance."}]}],"headings":[{"id":"pre-bound-field-components","text":"Pre-bound Field Components","level":2},{"id":"breaking-big-forms-into-smaller-pieces","text":"Breaking big forms into smaller pieces","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\nA common criticism of TanStack Form is its verbosity out-of-the-box. While this _can_ be useful for educational purposes - helping enforce understanding our APIs - it's not ideal in production use cases.\n\nAs a result, while basic usage of `[tanstackField]` enables the most powerful and flexible usage of TanStack Form, we provide APIs that wrap it and make your application code less verbose.\n\n## Pre-bound Field Components\n\nIf you've ever used TanStack Form in Angular to bind more than one input, you'll have quickly realized how much goes into each input:\n\n```angular-ts\nimport { Component } from '@angular/core'\nimport { TanStackField, injectForm, injectStore } from '@tanstack/angular-form'\n\n@Component({\n  selector: 'app-root',\n  standalone: true,\n  imports: [TanStackField],\n  template: `\n    <div>\n      <ng-container [tanstackField]=\"form\" name=\"firstName\" #firstName=\"field\">\n        <label [for]=\"firstName.api.name\">First Name:</label>\n        <input\n          [id]=\"firstName.api.name\"\n          [name]=\"firstName.api.name\"\n          [value]=\"firstName.api.state.value\"\n          (blur)=\"firstName.api.handleBlur()\"\n          (input)=\"firstName.api.handleChange($any($event).target.value)\"\n        />\n        @if (firstName.api.state.meta.isTouched) {\n          @for (error of firstName.api.state.meta.errors; track $index) {\n            <div style=\"color: red\">\n              {{ error }}\n            </div>\n          }\n        }\n        @if (firstName.api.state.meta.isValidating) {\n          <p>Validating...</p>\n        }\n      </ng-container>\n    </div>\n    <div>\n      <ng-container [tanstackField]=\"form\" name=\"lastName\" #lastName=\"field\">\n        <label [for]=\"lastName.api.name\">Last Name:</label>\n        <input\n          [id]=\"lastName.api.name\"\n          [name]=\"lastName.api.name\"\n          [value]=\"lastName.api.state.value\"\n          (blur)=\"lastName.api.handleBlur()\"\n          (input)=\"lastName.api.handleChange($any($event).target.value)\"\n        />\n        @if (lastName.api.state.meta.isTouched) {\n          @for (error of lastName.api.state.meta.errors; track $index) {\n            <div style=\"color: red\">\n              {{ error }}\n            </div>\n          }\n        }\n        @if (lastName.api.state.meta.isValidating) {\n          <p>Validating...</p>\n        }\n      </ng-container>\n    </div>\n  `,\n})\nexport class AppComponent {\n  form = injectForm({\n    defaultValues: {\n      firstName: '',\n      lastName: '',\n    },\n    onSubmit({ value }) {\n      // Do something with form data\n      console.log(value)\n    },\n  })\n}\n```\n\nThis is functionally correct, but introduces a _lot_ of repeated templating behavior over and over. Instead, let's move the error handling, label to input binding, and other repeated logic into a component:\n\n```angular-ts\nimport { injectField } from '@tanstack/angular-form'\n\n@Component({\n  selector: 'app-text-field',\n  standalone: true,\n  template: `\n    <label [for]=\"field.api.name\">{{ label() }}</label>\n    <input\n      [id]=\"field.api.name\"\n      [name]=\"field.api.name\"\n      [value]=\"field.api.state.value\"\n      (blur)=\"field.api.handleBlur()\"\n      (input)=\"field.api.handleChange($any($event).target.value)\"\n    />\n    @if (field.api.state.meta.isTouched) {\n      @for (error of field.api.state.meta.errors; track $index) {\n        <div style=\"color: red\">\n          {{ error }}\n        </div>\n      }\n    }\n    @if (field.api.state.meta.isValidating) {\n      <p>Validating...</p>\n    }\n  `,\n})\nexport class AppTextField {\n  label = input.required<string>()\n  // This API requires another part to it from the parent component\n  field = injectField<string>()\n}\n```\n\n> `injectField` accepts a single generic to define the `field.state.value` type.\n>\n> As a result, a numerical text field would be represented as `injectField<number>`, for example.\n\nNow, we can use the `TanStackAppField` directive (`tanstack-app-field`) to `provide` the expected field associated with this input:\n\n```angular-ts\nimport { Component } from '@angular/core'\nimport {\n  TanStackAppField,\n  TanStackField,\n  injectForm,\n} from '@tanstack/angular-form'\n\n@Component({\n  selector: 'app-root',\n  standalone: true,\n  imports: [TanStackField, TanStackAppField, AppTextField],\n  template: `\n    <div>\n      <app-text-field\n        label=\"First name:\"\n        tanstack-app-field\n        [tanstackField]=\"form\"\n        name=\"firstName\"\n      />\n    </div>\n    <div>\n      <app-text-field\n        label=\"Last name:\"\n        tanstack-app-field\n        [tanstackField]=\"form\"\n        name=\"lastName\"\n      />\n    </div>\n  `,\n})\nexport class AppComponent {\n  form = injectForm({\n    defaultValues: {\n      firstName: '',\n      lastName: '',\n    },\n    onSubmit({ value }) {\n      // Do something with form data\n      console.log(value)\n    },\n  })\n}\n```\n\n> Here, the `tanstack-app-field` directive is taking the properties from `[tanstackField]` and `provide`ing them down to the `app-text-field` so that they can be more easily consumed as a component.\n\n## Breaking big forms into smaller pieces\n\nSometimes forms get very large; it's just how it goes sometimes. While TanStack Form supports large forms well, it's never fun to work with hundreds or thousands of lines of code in a single component.\n\nTo solve this, we support breaking forms into smaller pieces using the `[tanstack-with-form]` directive together with the `injectWithForm` function.\n\nThe parent component owns the `form` (created via `injectForm`) and passes it down to a child component using the `tanstack-with-form` directive. The child component reads it back via `injectWithForm`, which returns a fully-typed reference to that same `FormApi` — meaning the child can render `[tanstackField]` bindings, `tanstack-app-field` components, etc. against the parent's form without needing to redeclare any generics.\n\nFirst, lift your shared form options out using `formOptions` so both the parent and the child can reference the same shape:\n\n```angular-ts\n// shared-form.ts\nimport { formOptions } from '@tanstack/angular-form'\n\nexport const peopleFormOpts = formOptions({\n  defaultValues: {\n    firstName: '',\n    lastName: '',\n  },\n})\n```\n\nThen, build a child component that consumes the form via `injectWithForm`:\n\n```angular-ts\n// child-form.component.ts\nimport { Component } from '@angular/core'\nimport {\n  TanStackAppField,\n  TanStackField,\n  injectWithForm,\n} from '@tanstack/angular-form'\nimport { AppTextField } from './app-text-field.component'\nimport { peopleFormOpts } from './shared-form'\n\n@Component({\n  selector: 'app-child-form',\n  standalone: true,\n  imports: [TanStackField, TanStackAppField, AppTextField],\n  template: `\n    <app-text-field\n      label=\"First name:\"\n      tanstack-app-field\n      [tanstackField]=\"withForm.form\"\n      name=\"firstName\"\n    />\n    <app-text-field\n      label=\"Last name:\"\n      tanstack-app-field\n      [tanstackField]=\"withForm.form\"\n      name=\"lastName\"\n    />\n  `,\n})\nexport class ChildForm {\n  // Spreading the form options into `injectWithForm` is what gives `withForm.form`\n  // its full type inference — no generics needed.\n  withForm = injectWithForm({ ...peopleFormOpts })\n}\n```\n\n> The options passed to `injectWithForm({ ...peopleFormOpts })` are only used for type inference. They are not read at runtime; the actual `FormApi` instance comes from the ancestor `tanstack-with-form` directive.\n\nFinally, in the parent component, create the form with `injectForm` and pass it to the child via the `tanstack-with-form` directive:\n\n```angular-ts\n// app.component.ts\nimport { Component } from '@angular/core'\nimport { TanStackWithForm, injectForm } from '@tanstack/angular-form'\nimport { ChildForm } from './child-form.component'\nimport { peopleFormOpts } from './shared-form'\n\n@Component({\n  selector: 'app-root',\n  standalone: true,\n  imports: [TanStackWithForm, ChildForm],\n  template: `\n    <form (submit)=\"handleSubmit($event)\">\n      <app-child-form tanstack-with-form [form]=\"form\" />\n      <button type=\"submit\">Submit</button>\n    </form>\n  `,\n})\nexport class AppComponent {\n  form = injectForm({\n    ...peopleFormOpts,\n    onSubmit({ value }) {\n      console.log(value)\n    },\n  })\n\n  handleSubmit(event: SubmitEvent) {\n    event.preventDefault()\n    event.stopPropagation()\n    this.form.handleSubmit()\n  }\n}\n```\n\nThis pattern lets you split a large form across many components while keeping a single source of truth for the form's state and types. Any descendant of the `tanstack-with-form` directive can call `injectWithForm({ ...peopleFormOpts })` to gain typed access to the same form instance.\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\nid: form-composition\ntitle: Form Composition\n---\n\nA common criticism of TanStack Form is its verbosity out-of-the-box. While this _can_ be useful for educational purposes - helping enforce understanding our APIs - it's not ideal in production use cases.\n\nAs a result, while basic usage of `[tanstackField]` enables the most powerful and flexible usage of TanStack Form, we provide APIs that wrap it and make your application code less verbose.\n\n## Pre-bound Field Components\n\nIf you've ever used TanStack Form in Angular to bind more than one input, you'll have quickly realized how much goes into each input:\n\n```angular-ts\nimport { Component } from '@angular/core'\nimport { TanStackField, injectForm, injectStore } from '@tanstack/angular-form'\n\n@Component({\n  selector: 'app-root',\n  standalone: true,\n  imports: [TanStackField],\n  template: `\n    <div>\n      <ng-container [tanstackField]=\"form\" name=\"firstName\" #firstName=\"field\">\n        <label [for]=\"firstName.api.name\">First Name:</label>\n        <input\n          [id]=\"firstName.api.name\"\n          [name]=\"firstName.api.name\"\n          [value]=\"firstName.api.state.value\"\n          (blur)=\"firstName.api.handleBlur()\"\n          (input)=\"firstName.api.handleChange($any($event).target.value)\"\n        />\n        @if (firstName.api.state.meta.isTouched) {\n          @for (error of firstName.api.state.meta.errors; track $index) {\n            <div style=\"color: red\">\n              {{ error }}\n            </div>\n          }\n        }\n        @if (firstName.api.state.meta.isValidating) {\n          <p>Validating...</p>\n        }\n      </ng-container>\n    </div>\n    <div>\n      <ng-container [tanstackField]=\"form\" name=\"lastName\" #lastName=\"field\">\n        <label [for]=\"lastName.api.name\">Last Name:</label>\n        <input\n          [id]=\"lastName.api.name\"\n          [name]=\"lastName.api.name\"\n          [value]=\"lastName.api.state.value\"\n          (blur)=\"lastName.api.handleBlur()\"\n          (input)=\"lastName.api.handleChange($any($event).target.value)\"\n        />\n        @if (lastName.api.state.meta.isTouched) {\n          @for (error of lastName.api.state.meta.errors; track $index) {\n            <div style=\"color: red\">\n              {{ error }}\n            </div>\n          }\n        }\n        @if (lastName.api.state.meta.isValidating) {\n          <p>Validating...</p>\n        }\n      </ng-container>\n    </div>\n  `,\n})\nexport class AppComponent {\n  form = injectForm({\n    defaultValues: {\n      firstName: '',\n      lastName: '',\n    },\n    onSubmit({ value }) {\n      // Do something with form data\n      console.log(value)\n    },\n  })\n}\n```\n\nThis is functionally correct, but introduces a _lot_ of repeated templating behavior over and over. Instead, let's move the error handling, label to input binding, and other repeated logic into a component:\n\n```angular-ts\nimport { injectField } from '@tanstack/angular-form'\n\n@Component({\n  selector: 'app-text-field',\n  standalone: true,\n  template: `\n    <label [for]=\"field.api.name\">{{ label() }}</label>\n    <input\n      [id]=\"field.api.name\"\n      [name]=\"field.api.name\"\n      [value]=\"field.api.state.value\"\n      (blur)=\"field.api.handleBlur()\"\n      (input)=\"field.api.handleChange($any($event).target.value)\"\n    />\n    @if (field.api.state.meta.isTouched) {\n      @for (error of field.api.state.meta.errors; track $index) {\n        <div style=\"color: red\">\n          {{ error }}\n        </div>\n      }\n    }\n    @if (field.api.state.meta.isValidating) {\n      <p>Validating...</p>\n    }\n  `,\n})\nexport class AppTextField {\n  label = input.required<string>()\n  // This API requires another part to it from the parent component\n  field = injectField<string>()\n}\n```\n\n> `injectField` accepts a single generic to define the `field.state.value` type.\n>\n> As a result, a numerical text field would be represented as `injectField<number>`, for example.\n\nNow, we can use the `TanStackAppField` directive (`tanstack-app-field`) to `provide` the expected field associated with this input:\n\n```angular-ts\nimport { Component } from '@angular/core'\nimport {\n  TanStackAppField,\n  TanStackField,\n  injectForm,\n} from '@tanstack/angular-form'\n\n@Component({\n  selector: 'app-root',\n  standalone: true,\n  imports: [TanStackField, TanStackAppField, AppTextField],\n  template: `\n    <div>\n      <app-text-field\n        label=\"First name:\"\n        tanstack-app-field\n        [tanstackField]=\"form\"\n        name=\"firstName\"\n      />\n    </div>\n    <div>\n      <app-text-field\n        label=\"Last name:\"\n        tanstack-app-field\n        [tanstackField]=\"form\"\n        name=\"lastName\"\n      />\n    </div>\n  `,\n})\nexport class AppComponent {\n  form = injectForm({\n    defaultValues: {\n      firstName: '',\n      lastName: '',\n    },\n    onSubmit({ value }) {\n      // Do something with form data\n      console.log(value)\n    },\n  })\n}\n```\n\n> Here, the `tanstack-app-field` directive is taking the properties from `[tanstackField]` and `provide`ing them down to the `app-text-field` so that they can be more easily consumed as a component.\n\n## Breaking big forms into smaller pieces\n\nSometimes forms get very large; it's just how it goes sometimes. While TanStack Form supports large forms well, it's never fun to work with hundreds or thousands of lines of code in a single component.\n\nTo solve this, we support breaking forms into smaller pieces using the `[tanstack-with-form]` directive together with the `injectWithForm` function.\n\nThe parent component owns the `form` (created via `injectForm`) and passes it down to a child component using the `tanstack-with-form` directive. The child component reads it back via `injectWithForm`, which returns a fully-typed reference to that same `FormApi` — meaning the child can render `[tanstackField]` bindings, `tanstack-app-field` components, etc. against the parent's form without needing to redeclare any generics.\n\nFirst, lift your shared form options out using `formOptions` so both the parent and the child can reference the same shape:\n\n```angular-ts\n// shared-form.ts\nimport { formOptions } from '@tanstack/angular-form'\n\nexport const peopleFormOpts = formOptions({\n  defaultValues: {\n    firstName: '',\n    lastName: '',\n  },\n})\n```\n\nThen, build a child component that consumes the form via `injectWithForm`:\n\n```angular-ts\n// child-form.component.ts\nimport { Component } from '@angular/core'\nimport {\n  TanStackAppField,\n  TanStackField,\n  injectWithForm,\n} from '@tanstack/angular-form'\nimport { AppTextField } from './app-text-field.component'\nimport { peopleFormOpts } from './shared-form'\n\n@Component({\n  selector: 'app-child-form',\n  standalone: true,\n  imports: [TanStackField, TanStackAppField, AppTextField],\n  template: `\n    <app-text-field\n      label=\"First name:\"\n      tanstack-app-field\n      [tanstackField]=\"withForm.form\"\n      name=\"firstName\"\n    />\n    <app-text-field\n      label=\"Last name:\"\n      tanstack-app-field\n      [tanstackField]=\"withForm.form\"\n      name=\"lastName\"\n    />\n  `,\n})\nexport class ChildForm {\n  // Spreading the form options into `injectWithForm` is what gives `withForm.form`\n  // its full type inference — no generics needed.\n  withForm = injectWithForm({ ...peopleFormOpts })\n}\n```\n\n> The options passed to `injectWithForm({ ...peopleFormOpts })` are only used for type inference. They are not read at runtime; the actual `FormApi` instance comes from the ancestor `tanstack-with-form` directive.\n\nFinally, in the parent component, create the form with `injectForm` and pass it to the child via the `tanstack-with-form` directive:\n\n```angular-ts\n// app.component.ts\nimport { Component } from '@angular/core'\nimport { TanStackWithForm, injectForm } from '@tanstack/angular-form'\nimport { ChildForm } from './child-form.component'\nimport { peopleFormOpts } from './shared-form'\n\n@Component({\n  selector: 'app-root',\n  standalone: true,\n  imports: [TanStackWithForm, ChildForm],\n  template: `\n    <form (submit)=\"handleSubmit($event)\">\n      <app-child-form tanstack-with-form [form]=\"form\" />\n      <button type=\"submit\">Submit</button>\n    </form>\n  `,\n})\nexport class AppComponent {\n  form = injectForm({\n    ...peopleFormOpts,\n    onSubmit({ value }) {\n      console.log(value)\n    },\n  })\n\n  handleSubmit(event: SubmitEvent) {\n    event.preventDefault()\n    event.stopPropagation()\n    this.form.handleSubmit()\n  }\n}\n```\n\nThis pattern lets you split a large form across many components while keeping a single source of truth for the form's state and types. Any descendant of the `tanstack-with-form` directive can call `injectWithForm({ ...peopleFormOpts })` to gain typed access to the same form instance.\n"}
